{"format":1,"key":"zone:desolace","path":"/lore/zone/desolace","name":"Desolace","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"desolace","name":"Desolace","path":"/lore/zone/desolace"},"levels":"","description":"Desolace is a bleak, windswept desert on Kalimdor's western coast, defined by cracked gray earth, constant stormy skies, and the bones of fallen beasts.…","intro":["Desolace is a bleak, windswept desert on Kalimdor's western coast, defined by cracked gray earth, constant stormy skies, and the bones of fallen beasts. It is the ancestral cradle of the vicious centaur race and a contested wasteland scarred by ancient Highborne ruins, encroaching demonic cults, and bitter tribal warfare. Both the Horde and Alliance maintain precarious footholds amidst the dust, each seeking to carve out influence while warding off spreading corruption."],"sections":[{"t":"A Land Cursed and Broken","p":["Desolace was not always a barren expanse of ash and yellowed pools. Legend holds that the land withered when the earth elemental Princess Theradras drained the surrounding life force to regenerate her form. Zaetar, son of Cenarius, came to her, but rather than subduing her, he took the princess as his mate. From their unnatural union sprang the first centaur. In shame and bloodthirsty wrath, the newborn race murdered their father and overran the plains, leaving behind the scarred wasteland known today."]},{"t":"Warring Hooves","p":["The interior of Desolace echoes with the thunder of thousands of hooves as four splintered centaur tribes wage endless war against all interlopers and each other. The Kolkar roam the eastern cliffs, the Magram hold crude yurts around brackish sinkholes, the Gelkis dwell behind rope bridges in deep southern ravines, and the fanatical Maraudine defend the approach to Maraudon itself. Travelers venturing across the wastes frequently find themselves drawn into this ancient blood feud, forced to slaughter one tribe to gain safe passage and tenuous parley with another."]},{"t":"Cults and Shadowed Coasts","p":["Beyond the warring centaur, darker perils fester along the borders. The Burning Blade cult operates freely out of Thunder Axe Fortress and Shadowbreak Ravine, summoning demons and satyrs that threaten to drown the region in fel fire. Along the stormy shoreline, naga creep onto the beaches of Ethel Rethor, while Darkspear trolls spear fish from the stilted platforms of Shadowprey Village. Tucked high in the northern crags, the Alliance watches from Nijel's Point, suspicious of the Horde's expansion and ever wary of the demonic taint spreading from Mannoroc Coven."]}],"clips":[],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Desolace (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Desolace_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Desolace","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Desolace"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/nijel-s-point","n":"Nijel's Point","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/shadowprey-village","n":"Shadowprey Village","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/kodo-graveyard","n":"Kodo Graveyard","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/gelkis-village","n":"Gelkis Village","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/magram-village","n":"Magram Village","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/thunder-axe-fortress","n":"Thunder Axe Fortress","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/mannoroc-coven","n":"Mannoroc Coven","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/stonetalon","n":"Stonetalon Mountains","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/roetten-stonehammer","n":"Roetten Stonehammer","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1453-reclaimers-business-in-desolace","n":"Reclaimers' Business in Desolace","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/4021-counterattack","n":"Counterattack!","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/79192-stepping-stones","n":"Stepping Stones","k":"quest"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/bolgan-s-hole","n":"Bolgan's Hole","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/ethel-rethor","n":"Ethel Rethor","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/gelkis-village","n":"Gelkis Village","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/s